      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T13:42:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion. This is existing entity-manager behaviour, the top-level interface has always carried these three properties, but I\u0027m happy to change it if we want to. A single `xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.Probe` exposed unconditionally is nicer than one interface per type.\n\nMy thinking is that the `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.\u003cType\u003e` interfaces should stay, since bmcweb uses them to find its targets and follows the associations on `Inventory.Item.Board` to reach the devices on the board (processors and so on). So Item.\u003cType\u003e remains the inventory marker and its associations, and Name/Type/Probe move to `Configuration.Probe`. Does that match what you had in mind?",
